perf(checkout): cap the payments client connection pool

The checkout pods have been creeping up against their memory limit and
were OOMKilled twice last week. Each idle keepalive connection to
payments-gateway holds a read buffer, and we allow 20 per pod across 12
pods -- far more than the gateway needs at our volume.

Dropping to 2 keeps steady-state memory comfortably under the limit.
Load tested at 5 rps with no change in latency.

Refs: PLAT-4471
